dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.over.link]/6-7: function templates whose template-heads are
not equivalent -- here they differ only in the condition of the
enable_if type of a defaulted constant template parameter -- are
distinct overloads, and [temp.deduct.general]/5,8: substituting the
explicitly specified arguments (and the defaults) into one of them may
fail, which only removes that candidate.  The front end keeps the
second template as the `#sfinae_alt' of the first and tried it only for
calls deducing from function arguments; with explicit template
arguments (`f<char>()') the first failed and the call had no candidate
("found no match for symbol 'f'").  Fails on the round-163 build bin52.
